  "details": "Ever since the may 3rd update, voice audio works while people are loading, then drops completely when they load.\nOnce loaded, all users are also moving like they are experiencing low framerate and cannot hear my own voice audio. World audio is unaffected.\nThe log appears relatively normal during all points up to this message which tends to coincide with the loss of voice:\n2021.05.07 02:23:49 Log - [Behaviour] uSpeak [1][938508098]: Segment playback time didn't match audio data length, audio cpu usage may be too high! - playbackTimeMS/audioLengthMS: 1115/600\n\n2021.05.07 02:23:49 Log - [Behaviour] uSpeak [18][938508099]: Segment playback time didn't match audio data length, audio cpu usage may be too high! - playbackTimeMS/audioLengthMS: 1116/820\n\nExpected: all users in an instance to load, move fluidly, and be able to hear and speak\n\nBuild 1089 did not correct this issue",
